This raises the whole topic of more-interesting artifact weapons. For
instance, Stormbringer could be made *much* more interesting. On the plus
side, it could act like a ring of (vampiric) regeneration. On the minus side,
Stormbringer should often attack peaceful creatures (like shopkeepers!) by
itself.

One way to simulate Stormbringer's willfulness would be to automatically set
the "safe pets" and "ask before attacking peaceful monsters" flags to FALSE
whenever Stormbringer is wielded. As in:

"Do you really want to attack Asidonhopo [y/n]? n"
"Against your will, the black sword lashes out! You hit!"
"It hits. It hits. It hits. Asidonhopo comes and takes all you possessions."

Stormbringer might also act as a cursed luckstone. Think about it.

